From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:27:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 308/311] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API AVS2 hwaccel

Add a V4L2 Request API hwaccel for the native AVS2 decoder, using the
stateless AVS2 uAPI of the Allwinner H616 cedrus driver: the OUTPUT
format V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS2_FRAME, one coded picture (picture header and
all slices, with their start codes) per request, and the SEQUENCE,
PICTURE, WEIGHT_QUANT and ALF controls. The reference list is passed
resolved, in reference configuration set order, with every reference's
own reference POC list, its picture type and the background flag; the
weighting quantization matrices are the final ones for the picture.

The sequence control is set at init so that the driver knows the bit
depth before the CAPTURE format is chosen (NV12 for Main, P010 for
Main10) and can refuse the size or the coding tools early.

The uAPI is not upstream yet; v4l2-stateless-avs2.h carries a private
copy of its definitions, skipped when the kernel headers provide them,
in the same way as the MPEG-4 and VC-1 hwaccels.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
